  "monitoring": [
    "FBC, renal function, and LFTs before each cycle",
    "Neurological assessment before each cycle (vincristine neuropathy monitoring)",
    "Pulmonary function monitoring — withhold bleomycin if new pulmonary symptoms develop",
    "Cardiac function (LVEF) monitoring — cumulative doxorubicin cardiotoxicity risk",
    "Cumulative doxorubicin dose tracking (lifetime maximum 450 mg/m²)",
    "Cumulative bleomycin dose tracking (maximum 500,000 international units in patients <60 years; refer to SPC for older patients)",
    "Blood glucose monitoring during prednisolone (Days 1-14) — hyperglycaemia risk",
    "ANC monitoring from Day 9 to guide G-CSF duration"
  ],
  "warnings": [
    "G-CSF is MANDATORY — 5 doses on Days 9-13 of every cycle. Growth factors are mandatory as part of this regimen.",
    "Procarbazine has weak MAOI activity — avoid alcohol (disulfiram-like reaction) and tyramine-rich foods (wines, cheeses). Do not use with other MAOIs.",
    "Maximum vincristine dose is 2mg. NPSA/2008/RRR04 must be followed for IV vinca alkaloids.",
    "Maximum lifetime cumulative doxorubicin dose: 450 mg/m² (400 mg/m² if prior mediastinal/pericardial radiotherapy). Discontinue doxorubicin if cardiac failure develops.",
    "Bleomycin cumulative dose limit: 500,000 units in patients <60 years. Refer to SPC for older patients. Risk of bleomycin-induced pneumonitis is greater in patients >40 years, smokers, prior mediastinal radiotherapy, poor renal function, or on growth factors.",
    "TA-GvHD risk: irradiated blood products are REQUIRED for all Hodgkin lymphoma patients for life. Transfusion departments must be notified and patient issued with alert card.",
    "PCP prophylaxis (co-trimoxazole 960mg Mon/Wed/Fri) is MANDATORY throughout treatment.",
    "Aciclovir 400mg twice daily and fluconazole 100mg once daily are mandatory antiviral/antifungal prophylaxis.",
    "Allopurinol 300mg once daily for 7 days — cycle 1 only (TLS prophylaxis).",
    "Monitor pulmonary function — bleomycin pulmonary toxicity risk. Withhold bleomycin if new pulmonary symptoms develop until investigated.",
    "Etoposide — hypotension risk during infusion; infuse over minimum 60 minutes.",
    "Cyclophosphamide 1250 mg/m² — Level 1 (escalated) dose. See dose table for 5-level reduction scale if toxicity occurs.",
    "Cycles should be repeated on Day 22 provided WBC >2.5×10⁹/L AND platelets >80×10⁹/L. Day 8 drugs (vincristine, bleomycin) given on schedule regardless of blood counts.",
    "Protocol is for up to 8 cycles. ARIA sets 6 cycles by default — prescriber must confirm total number of cycles."
  ],
